    "id": "rate_half_ca_hankel_a1_first_degree_core_one_quadratic_gap_four_double_root_separated_correction_center_disjoint_overlap_cap_one",
    "title": "A=1 quadratic separated correction-center disjointness and overlap cap one",
    "status": "PROVED",
    "closure": "reduction of the separated heavy-row gate to at most two scalar coefficients",
    "statement": "In the separated double-root extremal profile, supp(b_0,b_1)=U contains every assigned-center actual error support, while the padded-heavy point x_* lies outside U. Thus a correction root at any of the three centers would make x_* a padded locator root and put that center in both S_B and g_*, contradicting separatedness. Hence gcd(S_B,Lambda)=1. At most one center is a g_* root by the exact center deficit sum, so j=deg gcd(Lambda,g_*S_B^2)<=1 and the nonzero correction-coprime heavy row has at most two scalar coefficients.",
